            },
            {
                "entry_id": "d155477f-c379-39d9-9453-f7769606e8ff",
                "word": "pandectist",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "93676bb6-6cf1-4434-a6c4-a43e2b9ed653",
                        "entry_id": "d155477f-c379-39d9-9453-f7769606e8ff",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pandectists"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da679a8c-87a1-3e80-8f8b-3c3deff21962",
                        "entry_id": "d155477f-c379-39d9-9453-f7769606e8ff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An expert on the Pandects compiled under the Roman emperor Justinian I."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b825442c-7975-4b27-be9b-efcedd00a5c8",
                                "sense_id": "da679a8c-87a1-3e80-8f8b-3c3deff21962",
                                "text": "Many of the pandectists, however, do not mention the ammus negotia aliena gerendi among the requirements of negotiorum gestio;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "633de04e-8ff5-4f0f-9a01-5f70c96522cf",
                                "sense_id": "da679a8c-87a1-3e80-8f8b-3c3deff21962",
                                "text": "The legal principles deduced from the textual material of the CIC by such leading pandectists as Georg Friedrich Puchta (1798–1846) and Bernhard Windscheid (1817–1892) were sometimes used as legal norms in courts of law."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a330d939-996c-4505-80b8-51ad79c2fc66",
                                "sense_id": "da679a8c-87a1-3e80-8f8b-3c3deff21962",
                                "text": "Windscheid is the prototype pandectist who together with his friend Jhering was probably the most influential lawyer for nineteenth-century German civil law."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c81b684-982e-3ea1-9dc8-583ffd67249d",
                        "entry_id": "d155477f-c379-39d9-9453-f7769606e8ff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A proponent or developer of a complete code of laws of a country, especially of the German pandestic law."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8732fe10-d564-476e-a398-778d1c04fa23",
                                "sense_id": "3c81b684-982e-3ea1-9dc8-583ffd67249d",
                                "text": "The scheme the pandectists sought was a scheme dominated by certain legal ideals and principles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e28e3fa-e614-4f5b-af41-7ff297a09dcb",
                                "sense_id": "3c81b684-982e-3ea1-9dc8-583ffd67249d",
                                "text": "No doubt the Roman law of the post-classical period, and English law from and after the career of Pollock, have tended to become more self-conscious and theoretical in character, but Roman law never reached a state at all comparable to that reached by the pandectists of the nineteenth century, nor has English law yet reached it, if it ever will."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71d67b01-81eb-4ed4-bfa9-f232b114ab8d",
                                "sense_id": "3c81b684-982e-3ea1-9dc8-583ffd67249d",
                                "text": "In turn, the German historical school and the pandectists, with their emphasis upon the absoluteness and exclusiveness of property, had an impact upon France."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "87d85713-fb13-4221-b6a3-bf3f83ad371c",
                                "sense_id": "3c81b684-982e-3ea1-9dc8-583ffd67249d",
                                "text": "It is an invention of the pandectists that there was no liability for others in Roman law unless the superior himself was at fault."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
